Build 3 features for Rankora at `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Rankora`: **ZIP Upload**, **Candidate Tags**, **Candidate Assignment**.

Read CLAUDE.md first. Then read:
- `src/components/BulkUploadZone.tsx` — current bulk upload (individual files only)
- `src/components/JobDetailView.tsx` — main job view with candidate list
- `src/components/CandidateRow.tsx` — candidate row rendering
- `src/components/CandidateDetailSheet.tsx` — candidate detail panel
- `src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx` — kanban cards
- `src/hooks/useTeam.tsx` — team members
- `package.json` — check if JSZip is installed

---

## Feature 1: ZIP Upload Support

### Install JSZip
Run: `npm install jszip` (or add it — check if it's already in package.json)

### Modify `src/components/BulkUploadZone.tsx`

Currently accepts individual files (PDF, DOCX, etc). Add ZIP support:

1. Add `.zip` to accepted file extensions and MIME types (`application/zip`, `application/x-zip-compressed`)
2. When a .zip file is dropped/selected:
   - Import JSZip dynamically: `const JSZip = (await import('jszip')).default;`
   - Read the ZIP: `const zip = await JSZip.loadAsync(file);`
   - Extract all files from the ZIP
   - Filter: only keep files with allowed resume extensions (PDF, DOCX, DOC, RTF, TXT)
   - Add extracted files to the upload queue (same as individual files)
   - Show toast: "Extracted X resumes from ZIP file"
   - Skip non-resume files silently (images, folders, etc.)

3. Update the drop zone text: "Drop resumes or ZIP files here"
4. Update accepted file info: "PDF, DOCX, DOC, RTF, TXT, or ZIP"

The extraction should happen BEFORE files enter the queue. The existing per-file upload logic handles the rest.

Key implementation in handleFileDrop/handleFileSelect:
```typescript
const processFiles = async (rawFiles: File[]) => {
  const resumeFiles: File[] = [];

  for (const file of rawFiles) {
    if (file.name.toLowerCase().endsWith('.zip')) {
      try {
        const JSZip = (await import('jszip')).default;
        const zip = await JSZip.loadAsync(file);
        for (const [path, zipEntry] of Object.entries(zip.files)) {
          if (zipEntry.dir) continue;
          const ext = path.split('.').pop()?.toLowerCase();
          if (!['pdf', 'docx', 'doc', 'rtf', 'txt'].includes(ext || '')) continue;
          const blob = await zipEntry.async('blob');
          const extractedFile = new File([blob], zipEntry.name.split('/').pop() || path, {
            type: getMimeType(ext || ''),
          });
          resumeFiles.push(extractedFile);
        }
        toast.success(`Extracted ${resumeFiles.length} resumes from ${file.name}`);
      } catch {
        toast.error(`Failed to extract ${file.name}`);
      }
    } else {
      resumeFiles.push(file);
    }
  }

  return resumeFiles;
};
```

Helper for MIME type:
```typescript
function getMimeType(ext: string): string {
  const map: Record<string, string> = {
    pdf: 'application/pdf',
    docx: 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document',
    doc: 'application/msword',
    rtf: 'application/rtf',
    txt: 'text/plain',
  };
  return map[ext] || 'application/octet-stream';
}
```

---

## Feature 2: Candidate Tags

### DB Migration — `supabase/migrations/20260409200000_candidate_tags_and_assignment.sql`

```sql
-- Candidate tags
CREATE TABLE public.candidate_tags (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  resume_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES public.resumes(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  job_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES public.jobs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  tag text NOT NULL,
  color text NOT NULL DEFAULT '#6366f1',
  created_by uuid REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,
  created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
  UNIQUE(resume_id, tag)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_candidate_tags_resume ON public.candidate_tags(resume_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_candidate_tags_job_tag ON public.candidate_tags(job_id, tag);
ALTER TABLE public.candidate_tags ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Team members of the job can manage tags
CREATE POLICY "Team can view tags" ON public.candidate_tags FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.jobs j LEFT JOIN public.team_members tm ON tm.team_id = j.team_id AND tm.user_id = auth.uid() WHERE j.id = candidate_tags.job_id AND (j.user_id = auth.uid() OR tm.user_id IS NOT NULL)));

CREATE POLICY "Team can manage tags" ON public.candidate_tags FOR ALL TO authenticated
  USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.jobs j LEFT JOIN public.team_members tm ON tm.team_id = j.team_id AND tm.user_id = auth.uid() WHERE j.id = candidate_tags.job_id AND (j.user_id = auth.uid() OR tm.user_id IS NOT NULL)));

-- Candidate assignment
ALTER TABLE public.resumes ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS assigned_to uuid REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL;
```

### Hook — `src/hooks/useCandidateTags.tsx`

```typescript
export function useCandidateTags(jobId: string | null) {
  // Fetch all tags for a job (grouped by resume_id)
  // Return: { tags: Map<string, Tag[]>, allTagNames: string[], addTag, removeTag, isLoading }
  // Realtime subscription on candidate_tags filtered by job_id
}
```

### Component — `src/components/candidate/CandidateTagInput.tsx`

Props: `resumeId: string, jobId: string, existingTags: Tag[], allTagNames: string[]`

Features:
- Shows existing tags as colored chips with X to remove
- Input field: type to add new tag or select from existing (autocomplete from allTagNames)
- Preset color palette (6 colors: blue, green, amber, red, violet, slate)
- Common preset tags shown as suggestions: "Shortlisted", "On Hold", "Top Choice", "Follow Up", "Culture Fit", "Overqualified"
- On enter or click suggestion: adds tag
- On X: removes tag

### Integration

**CandidateRow.tsx** — Show tag chips next to candidate name. Small colored badges.

**CandidateDetailSheet.tsx** — Full tag input in the detail panel.

**KanbanBoard.tsx** — Show first 2 tags on cards (truncated if more).

**JobDetailView.tsx** — Add tag filter: dropdown to filter candidates by tag. Wire `useCandidateTags` hook and pass data to children.

**Bulk action** — The existing bulk action bar in JobDetailView should include "Add Tag" option. When clicked, show a popover to select/type a tag, then add it to all selected candidates.

---

## Feature 3: Candidate Assignment to Team Members

### DB change already included in the migration above:
`ALTER TABLE public.resumes ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS assigned_to uuid REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL;`

### Component — `src/components/candidate/AssigneeSelector.tsx`

Props: `resumeId: string, currentAssignee: string | null, teamMembers: TeamMember[], onAssign: (userId: string | null) => void`

Features:
- Small dropdown/popover: "Assign to..." 
- Shows team members list with avatar initials
- Currently assigned member highlighted
- "Unassign" option
- On select: updates `resumes.assigned_to` via `(supabase as any)`

### Integration

